    "lawCode": "Add §88, State L",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3424\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the state law, in relation to a state slogan\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThe bill would codify \"I Love New York\" as the official state slogan.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 makes \"I Love New York\" the official state slogan.\n\nSection 2 makes the act take immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nNew York state has for years been using the phrase \"I Love NY\" in\nState promotions. The slogan has become one of the most recognizable\nproduct brands globally, and has been emulated domestically.\nUbiquitous in New York State, the slogan appears on thousands of\nproducts and promotions offered to both residents and tourists.\n\nThe State should take the symbolic step of recognizing our citizens'\nownership of the phrase \"I Love NY\" and codify it as our official\nState slogan.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nA.11478 of 2004; A.2841 of 2005-2006; A.4686 of 2007-2008 S.2841 of\n2005-2006; S.8140 of 2007-2008\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
